  "result": "All 5 tests pass.\n\n```\n.....                                                                    [100%]\n5 passed in 0.02s\n```\n\n**What I did:** added `bus/eventbus.py` with the `EventBus` class. Subscribers are kept per topic in subscription order, `subscribe` returns an idempotent unsubscribe closure, `publish` appends to a FIFO deque, and `flush` drains the deque until empty. Handler lists are snapshotted per event so subscribing or unsubscribing mid-dispatch does not disturb the event being handled. A re-entrant `flush` call from inside a handler returns immediately and lets the outer flush finish draining.\n\n**Approach chosen:** B, queued dispatch. It gives `flush` a real job rather than being a no-op, guarantees events published by handlers run after the current event finishes, and keeps stack depth bounded no matter how deeply handlers chain publishes.",
